prompt:
Implement a helmet impact damage simulation using Three.js. Load ScatteringSkull.glb, click the surface to simulate impacts that produce dents, and observe material changes and declining structural integrity.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following import map in <head>, and import via ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Model Loading]
(1) Use GLTFLoader to load assets/ScatteringSkull.glb;
(2) Display the model centered in the scene;

[Impact Interaction]
(3) Click the model surface using a Raycaster to add an impact point;
(4) Display the impact point as a red marker (small sphere with radius=0.02);
(5) For each impact, create a visual dent effect within a radius of 0.3 around the impact point (by scaling displacement or overlaying a decal);

[Material Degradation]
(6) After a cumulative total of 3 impacts, increase the overall material roughness by 0.2 (to simulate wear);
(7) For each impact, add a metalness variation in the impact area (to simulate surface damage);

[Structural Integrity]
(8) Initial integrity is 100%;
(9) Each impact reduces integrity by 10-15% (randomly);
(10) When integrity <= 30%, change the model to a red warning tint;
(11) When integrity <= 0%, display a "Structural Failure" warning;

[OrbitControls]
(12) Support rotating the view;

[HUD Display]
(13) HUD in the upper-left corner:
  - Impact count (id="impactCount")
  - Structural integrity (id="integrity", percentage)
  - Current roughness (id="roughness")

[State Exposure (Required)]
Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
  - modelLoaded: boolean
  - impactCount: number
  - integrity: number (0-100)
  - roughness: number
  - lastImpactPos: {x,y,z} (most recent impact position)

Output a single standalone HTML file.
